The function is already minimal, so this rewrite only changes how the compiler lays out the code; results are identical for every input. The `type` field is loaded into a local and the common path, where `type` is already set, is marked as the expected branch. The `profile` lookup becomes the cold path. Any speedup is likely small.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```